("ADR-002-frontend-framework.md", "Frontend framework", "Proposed", "Next.js/TypeScript is a user-preferred candidate for dashboard and BFF surfaces. Acceptance needs auth/session, accessibility, CSP and SSE proof in a non-financial spike."),
("ADR-003-modular-monolith-vs-microservices.md", "Modular monolith vs microservices", "Accepted for planning", "Use a modular monolith with owned persistence, dependency checks, transaction kernel and broker-neutral contracts. Extract only with workload/isolation/ownership evidence."),
("ADR-004-database.md", "Database", "Accepted for planning", "PostgreSQL is initial authoritative relational store for ledger, inbox/outbox, audit projections and tenant policies; no external broker without workload evidence."),
("ADR-005-internal-ledger.md", "Internal ledger", "Accepted for planning", "Use a singular immutable double-entry availability ledger; balances are derived from postings and external events never mutate availability directly."),
("ADR-006-custody.md", "Custody", "Proposed", "No custody model is legally selected. Evaluate hybrid/MPC/HSM/multisig/custodian under Q-001..Q-004; direct private-key storage is prohibited."),
("ADR-007-signing-infrastructure.md", "Signing infrastructure", "Proposed", "Per-operation signer request is guarded/decoded/allowlisted and binds authorization hash, scope and environment. Provider/key ceremony decision is evidence-gated."),
("ADR-008-ai-architecture.md", "AI architecture", "Accepted for planning", "AI emits bounded typed proposals only; no direct transaction, policy, allowlist, risk override or secret access. Multi-agent is optional analytical decomposition."),
("ADR-009-market-data-architecture.md", "Market data architecture", "Accepted for planning", "Use collectors/normalizer/snapshots/quality decisions. PostgreSQL first; cache/broker are derived infrastructure and never authority."),
("ADR-010-event-architecture.md", "Event architecture", "Accepted for planning", "Use versioned broker-neutral contracts with transactional PostgreSQL inbox/outbox and replay-safe consumer idempotency before a broker."),
("ADR-011-authentication.md", "Authentication", "Accepted for planning", "Passkey-first WebAuthn, session rotation, step-up for sensitive actions, tenant authorization and wallet proof as additional identity evidence only."),
("ADR-012-secrets.md", "Secrets", "Accepted for planning", "Secret values are external KMS/Vault-managed; application stores references/envelopes; logs, AI and audit use redaction."),
